<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.15.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01524</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.15.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e54236c4-913e-4fc3-9e4c-4578e808decb</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. Double click on mathematical
  expressions/equations to enlarge. If needed, use the “^” symbol to enter an exponent.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="54828607-798d-48f4-9098-8816f83d3f26" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Whenever the input of a function \(f\) increases by 1, the output increases by 5. Which of these equations
          could define \(f\)?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(x)=3x+5\)</para><para>\(f(x)=5x+3\)</para><para>\( f(x)=5^x\)</para><para>\( f(x)=x^5\) </para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.15.2. 
      </para><para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=5x+3\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="4c75059f-e45f-4203-9d6d-2787a3c8b931" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The function \(f\) is defined by \(f(x)=2^x\). Which of the following statements is true about the values of
          \(f\)? <emphasis>Select all </emphasis>that apply. </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is b and d. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="968c16ab-3a12-494b-9d43-4b32752c1cab" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The two lines on the coordinate plane are graphs of functions \(f\) and \(g\). Use for the graph below for
        questions 3 and 4.</para><para><figure><media alt="Graph of 2 lines."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/12724ad9231ed2d7dd1720cc90447eb9c5fa3e21"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Use the graph to explain why the value of \(f\) increases by 2 each time the input \(x\) increases by
          1. 
        </para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.15.2. 
      </para><para>The correct answer is: \((0,0)\) and \((1,2)\) are two points on the graph of \(f\). Between the two points,
        \(y\) increases by 2 and \(x\) increases by 1.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="a146c478-5f35-4970-b07d-8d9594463256" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Use the graph to explain why the value of \(g\) increases by 2 each time the input \(x\) increases by 1.
          <emphasis>Select two </emphasis>that apply.
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is a and d. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="1107dbf8-66fc-45a5-9745-97e5975d3473" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The function \(h\) is given by \(h(x)=5^x\). Find the quotient \(\frac{h(x+2)}{h(x)}\). 
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.15.3. 
      </para><para>The correct answer is 25. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="5674259f-b084-4426-bbff-5cf458fbcbd1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>The function \(h\) is given by \(h(x)=5^x\). Find the quotient \(\frac{h(x+3)}{h(x)}\).</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.15.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 125. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="68556bd3-af50-4ef9-b72b-3b62d0a83449" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each of the functions \(f,g,h,p\), and \(q\), the domain is \(0≤x≤100\). For which functions is
          the average rate of change a good measure of how the function changes for this domain? <emphasis>Select three</emphasis> that
          apply. </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.15.4. 
      </para><para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=x+2, h(x)=111x−23, q(x)=87.5\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="2ba83d50-cf33-400c-a317-9a186fa46fc3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What would be the rate of change of the following table?</para>
        <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>
                \(x\)
              </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
                \(f(x)\)
              </emphasis></entry></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                1
              </entry>
              <entry>
                -4
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                2
              </entry>
              <entry>
                -2
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                3
              </entry>
              <entry>
                0
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                4
              </entry>
              <entry>
                2
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                5
              </entry>
              <entry>
                4
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.15.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is 2.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="9c739c4f-ee63-4f46-bfdd-8ccfeb05fbc7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Given the following table, what would be \(\frac {f(x+2)}{f(x+1)}\)?</para>
        
        
        <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>
                \(x\)
              </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
                \(f(x)\)
              </emphasis></entry></row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                1
              </entry>
              <entry>
                2
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                2
              </entry>
              <entry>
                4
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                3
              </entry>
              <entry>
                8
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                4
              </entry>
              <entry>
                16
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                5
              </entry>
              <entry>
                32
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.15.3. 
      </para><para>The correct answer is 2.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="bf41e467-06b4-41c1-8496-accddf0ee0a0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which of the following statements compare rates of \(f(x) = 3x +2\) and \(g(x)=3^x\)?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>In \(f\) and \(g\) you multiply by 3 to get to the next term.</para><para>In \(f\) and \(g\) you add 3 to get to the next term.</para><para>In \(f\) you add 3 to get to the next term; in \(g\) you multiply by 3 to get to the next term.</para><para>In \(g\) you add 3 to get to the next term; in \(f\) you multiply by 3 to get to the next term.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try Again!</para><para>You seem to be struggling. Who can you ask for help?</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
